# Crossweb capability grants.
# The host loads this file from the process working directory at startup.
# One plugin.command per line. Commands that are not listed are denied.
# A line whose first character is # is a comment. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# app.ping is the sample shell's only grant. It returns a nonce and touches no
# files or secrets. fs.read and fs.write stay commented out. If they are
# uncommented later, path checks still confine them to the app data directory
# and reject symlinks. That confinement is not an OS sandbox.
app.ping
# fs.read
# fs.write
# keystore.encrypt
# keystore.decrypt
# keystore.save
# keystore.load
# keystore.get
